#HELPS

0 PRINCIPLE NINJATRAINING~
Syntax: principle
        principle <sora|chikyu|ningenno>
        principle <sora|chikyu|ningenno> improve
Displays Ninja tracks/available powers or buys the next rank.
Each track caps at 10. Training costs 10 times the next rank in primal.
Sora supplies awareness/shadow techniques; Chikyu preparation and control;
Ningenno weapon techniques and native combat passives.
WEB requires Chikyu 8 and 10 Ki, despite older rank-6 descriptions.
~

0 HUMBLE~
Syntax: humble <room target>
Ninja clan induction for a Ninja of native rank 3 or better.
The target must be another clanless Ninja with the native eligibility flag.
Copies your clan to the target, assigns Genin rank 4 and autosaves it.
It is not a hostile debuff or a way to turn another class into a Ninja.
~

0 PROMOTE~
Syntax: promote <room target>
Ninja clan command for native rank 2 or better.
Requires another player Ninja of the same clan; sets Chunin rank 3
and saves the target. Drow house promotion uses PROMOTION instead.
~

0 DEMOTE~
Syntax: demote <room target>
Ninja clan command for native rank 2 or better.
Requires another player Ninja of the same clan; sets Genin rank 4
and saves the target. Drow house demotion uses FAILURE instead.
~

0 MICHI~
Syntax: michi
Sora 1, 100 Ki. Sets native Michi energy to 25 times Sora rank.
The Ninja combat hooks use that energy; CALM ends the state.
There is additional native wait when invoked during combat.
This does not grant Werewolf breed/tribe powers despite the shared counter.
~

0 KAKUSU~
Syntax: kakusu
Sora 6. Activating shadow concealment costs 20 Ki and command wait.
Using it again removes that concealment without the activation charge.
Native movement/shadow-travel upkeep can consume Ki or reveal you.
This is separate from Mage invisibility and Vampire Obfuscate.
~

0 BOMUZITE~
Syntax: bomuzite <room target>
Sora 8, 20 Ki. Puts an eligible target to sleep and ends its combat.
Rejects self, group members, already sleeping/incapacitated targets,
protected staff, safe targets and non-PK player combat before charging.
It does not create a stored bomb item or damage every room occupant.
~

0 MIZOTAMOUYO~
Syntax: mizotamouyo <world target>
Sora 10. Shadow travel to an eligible target in a different room.
Players must permit SUMMON; native level, illusion and destination
safe/private/solitary exclusions apply. Both rooms' no-travel protections,
combat/timers, root/restraint, body/plane restrictions block the attempt.
If concealed with Kakusu, successful travel spends 20 Ki to maintain it;
insufficient Ki reveals you. Unconcealed travel has no such upkeep cost.
Invalid/protected attempts do not pay that concealment cost.
~

0 MIENAKU~
Syntax: mienaku
Chikyu 1, 20 Ki. Combat escape through an ordinary open adjacent exit.
Root, bindings and native restraint rules can stop it; an opposing
Get of Fenris Werewolf has its native chance to halt your escape.
A committed attempt costs 20 Ki even if no usable exit succeeds.
Success ends combat and can set the opponent's native blindfold state;
BLINDFOLD SELF removes that state when able to act.
This is physical exit movement, not world-target teleportation.
~

0 ORIMASU~
Syntax: orimasu
Chikyu 4, 50 Ki. Sets the native regeneration counter to 10.
Refuses without payment while that counter is already above 4.
The normal regeneration update uses the counter; this is not an
instant full heal or permanent maximum-health increase.
~

0 TSUMAZUKU~
Syntax: tsumazuku
Chikyu 8. Attempts to trip the current combat opponent.
The native roll can backfire and impose a longer wait on you.
Success imposes waits on both combatants; it does not permanently
change the target's raw stats or guarantee an automatic damage hit.
~

0 HARAKIRI~
Syntax: harakiri
Chikyu 10. Activates the native blood-ritual combat counter.
Requires at least one-fifth maximum health and no active prior ritual.
WARNING: health and mana are set to only one-twentieth of their maxima.
The counter is derived from pre-ritual health/mana and normal updates
govern it. This is a costly preparation, not a free heal or permanent buff.
~

0 TSUME~
Syntax: tsume
Ningenno 1. Toggles the native claws flag for Ninja wrist blades.
It does not create a new carried weapon or grant Vampire disciplines.
Native natural-weapon/combat hooks use the active flag.
~

0 SHUURAI~
Syntax: shuurai [room target]
Ningenno 4. Requires a piercing weapon in the weapon or held slot.
Uses a valid named room target, otherwise the current opponent.
Rejects self/native safe targets, performs the piercing circle attack
and applies its wait. A different weapon damage type does not qualify.
~

0 HAKUNETSU~
Syntax: hakunetsu <room target>
Ningenno 10. Requires a piercing weapon in the weapon or held slot.
Rejects self and an injured target already using a fighting stance.
After native safety checks it may activate eligible Kakusu concealment,
then performs the native backstab attack and applies its wait.
Automatic concealment can cost its normal 20 Ki; this is not a free
mastery bypass or guaranteed success against every opponent.
~

